            model: "Steel producers base output on their private costs (MPC). Pollution imposes external costs on local residents, so MSC lies above MPC. The market produces Qm, where MPB = MPC, but the socially optimal output is Qopt, where MSB = MSC. Between Qopt and Qm each unit costs society more than it is worth (MSC > MSB), so there is overproduction and the shaded triangle is the welfare loss.",
